WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:03.534
-And after three weeks
of humiliating chaos,

00:00:03.534 --> 00:00:05.767
Republicans finally elected
a speaker of the House

00:00:05.767 --> 00:00:08.167
who isn't just a far-right
election denier,

00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:10.200
but was actually one of
the architects of the effort

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.467
to overturn
the 2020 election results.

00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:15.767
The House GOP's decision
comes as Trump himself faces

00:00:15.767 --> 00:00:17.234
damning new legal developments

00:00:17.234 --> 00:00:19.334
in three separate cases
across the country,

00:00:19.334 --> 00:00:21.534
from Michael Cohen's
testimony in New York

00:00:21.534 --> 00:00:23.200
to Mark Meadows
testimony in DC

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.434
to one of his former attorneys
pleading guilty in Georgia.

00:00:25.434 --> 00:00:27.934
For more on this,
it's time for A Closer Look.

00:00:27.934 --> 00:00:30.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:32.067 --> 00:00:35.801
One thing I've never been able
to understand about Trump World

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:38.033
is how all these guys
handle the pressure of being

00:00:38.033 --> 00:00:40.334
in so much legal trouble
all the time.

00:00:40.334 --> 00:00:42.634
They all have one foot
in prison.

00:00:42.634 --> 00:00:45.234
They drink scotch like water
and eat nothing but steaks,

00:00:45.234 --> 00:00:46.834
and somehow
they're all doing fine.

00:00:46.834 --> 00:00:50.701
It's a real tribute to the
advances of modern cardiology.

00:00:50.701 --> 00:00:54.067
If I let my vehicle
registration lapse for a day,

00:00:54.067 --> 00:00:56.968
I get palpitations,
I can't feel my legs.

00:00:56.968 --> 00:00:59.834
One time I rear ended another
car in a Costco parking lot,

00:00:59.834 --> 00:01:03.167
got out, saw there was no damage
and just took off.

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:05.000
And I still have
nightmares about it.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:07.634
I just know I'm going
to be sitting on a beach

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:09.567
in Spain
when I'm 85 years old,

00:01:09.567 --> 00:01:11.801
and a Chicago cop
is going to walk up behind me

00:01:11.801 --> 00:01:13.667
and I'll say,
"What took you so long?"

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:15.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:17.133
The only thing keeping
my location a secret for now

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:20.400
is my show airs at 12:37 in
the morning and also on Peacock.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.634 --> 00:01:24.501
Take Trump, for example.

00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:26.334
I don't know why he said,
for example.

00:01:26.334 --> 00:01:28.601
He's "the" example.

00:01:28.601 --> 00:01:30.667
He's got four different
criminal cases,

00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:33.801
four examples
and a civil fraud trial.

00:01:33.801 --> 00:01:35.834
Well, this week there have been
three major developments

00:01:35.834 --> 00:01:37.100
in three separate
Trump cases.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:39.701
His former fixer testified
against him in New York.

00:01:39.701 --> 00:01:41.601
Another one of his lawyers
flipped on him in Georgia,

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.434
and we found out
his former chief of staff

00:01:43.434 --> 00:01:46.701
testified to the special counsel
in DC.

00:01:46.701 --> 00:01:48.667
-Breaking news tonight,
the former Trump

00:01:48.667 --> 00:01:50.667
White House Chief of Staff,
Mark Meadows,

00:01:50.667 --> 00:01:53.367
reportedly offering
damning testimony

00:01:53.367 --> 00:01:56.834
against the former president
to special counsel Jack Smith.

00:01:56.834 --> 00:01:58.467
-Breaking news out of New York.

00:01:58.467 --> 00:02:01.167
Former President Donald Trump
came face to face

00:02:01.167 --> 00:02:03.234
with his
former personal attorney

00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:05.567
and longtime fixer,
Michael Cohen,

00:02:05.567 --> 00:02:07.767
for the first time
in five years

00:02:07.767 --> 00:02:09.801
inside a courtroom
in New York today,

00:02:09.801 --> 00:02:12.534
Cohen is testifying as part
of the civil fraud case

00:02:12.534 --> 00:02:14.100
against Trump
and his company.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:17.868
-Breaking news out of Georgia,
where just this morning,

00:02:17.868 --> 00:02:19.367
former Trump attorney
Jenna Ellis

00:02:19.367 --> 00:02:23.267
pleaded guilty in the state's
2020 election interference case.

00:02:23.267 --> 00:02:25.334
Ellis is now
the fourth defendant

00:02:25.334 --> 00:02:27.300
to accept a plea deal
with prosecutors.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:29.467
-When it comes
to Trump's legal troubles,

00:02:29.467 --> 00:02:31.634
they're going to have to break
into breaking news stories,

00:02:31.634 --> 00:02:33.100
with more breaking news.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:34.334
-Breaking news tonight
the former

00:02:34.334 --> 00:02:36.167
Trump White House
Chief of Staff...

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:37.834
-Breaking news out of New York.

00:02:37.834 --> 00:02:40.234
Former President Donald Trump
came face to...

00:02:40.234 --> 00:02:43.968
-Breaking news out of Georgia,
where just this morning,

00:02:43.968 --> 00:02:46.033
former Trump attorney
Jenna Ellis pleaded guilt...

00:02:46.033 --> 00:02:47.567
Breaking news
out of Sheboygan,

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:49.868
where Donald Trump has
just been caught shoplifting,

00:02:49.868 --> 00:02:52.634
an Us Weekly
out of a Piggly Wiggly.

00:02:52.634 --> 00:02:54.300
[ As Donald Trump ]
If I'm guilty of anything,

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:55.501
it's wanting to catch up

00:02:55.501 --> 00:02:57.534
on the latest with Taylor
and Travis,

00:02:57.534 --> 00:02:58.701
team...

00:02:58.701 --> 00:03:01.133
Team both of them.
So wholesome, so sweet.

00:03:01.133 --> 00:03:03.567
She's there with the mother,
and he supports her career.

00:03:03.567 --> 00:03:05.934
It's just a beautiful thing.
And if there's if there's

00:03:05.934 --> 00:03:07.434
one thing
everyone knows about Trump,

00:03:07.434 --> 00:03:10.000
it's that I love love.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.501
Also, I stole a bunch
of Kit-Kats

00:03:11.501 --> 00:03:14.133
because I also love candy.

00:03:14.133 --> 00:03:16.434
[ Normal voice ] So let's take
these one at a time.

00:03:16.434 --> 00:03:18.534
First, there's Michael Cohen,
who testified yesterday

00:03:18.534 --> 00:03:20.267
and again today
in a Manhattan courtroom

00:03:20.267 --> 00:03:22.701
where Trump is at risk
of losing his business empire

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:24.000
in a fraud suit

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.334
brought by New York Attorney
General Letitia James.

00:03:26.334 --> 00:03:27.968
Trump was actually
in the courtroom face

00:03:27.968 --> 00:03:28.968
to face with Cohen,

00:03:28.968 --> 00:03:30.467
as Cohen detailed
the various ways

00:03:30.467 --> 00:03:32.667
in which Trump told him
to commit fraud

00:03:32.667 --> 00:03:35.033
by lying about the value
of his company's assets.

00:03:35.033 --> 00:03:36.734
-Former President
Donald Trump watched

00:03:36.734 --> 00:03:38.834
as his former personal attorney,
Michael Cohen,

00:03:38.834 --> 00:03:40.868
testified against him
in New York's lawsuit

00:03:40.868 --> 00:03:42.267
over Trump's businesses.

00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:44.334
-NBC News reporting this,

00:03:44.334 --> 00:03:46.033
Cohen said,
"Trump would come up

00:03:46.033 --> 00:03:48.267
with his own net
worth estimations."

00:03:48.267 --> 00:03:50.734
"My responsibility,
along with Allen Weisselberg,

00:03:50.734 --> 00:03:53.567
predominantly,
was to reverse engineer

00:03:53.567 --> 00:03:55.667
the various
different asset classes

00:03:55.667 --> 00:03:58.934
and increase those assets
in order to achieve a number

00:03:58.934 --> 00:04:01.167
that Trump asked us for,"
he said.

00:04:01.167 --> 00:04:03.400
Asked what that number would be,

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:06.901
Cohen said, quote,
"Whatever number he told us."

00:04:06.901 --> 00:04:09.167
-So Trump would literally
just invent a number

00:04:09.167 --> 00:04:10.400
for the value
of his assets

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:11.968
or his net worth
out of thin air.

00:04:11.968 --> 00:04:13.868
Then tell his minions
to fudge the math

00:04:13.868 --> 00:04:15.434
in order to make
that number work.

00:04:15.434 --> 00:04:16.901
That would explain
why his net worth

00:04:16.901 --> 00:04:22.067
was always some very round
clean number, like $10 billion.

00:04:22.067 --> 00:04:26.400
No one has a net worth.
That's exactly $10 billion.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:28.167
Usually there's at least
one decimal point.

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:29.300
It's like getting a fake ID

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:30.601
that says your 21st birthday

00:04:30.601 --> 00:04:31.934
is "today."

00:04:31.934 --> 00:04:33.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.601 --> 00:04:35.534
[ High-pitched voice ] That's
right, my birthday is today.

00:04:35.534 --> 00:04:38.033
And that's why I need these
key-lime flavored wine coolers.

00:04:38.033 --> 00:04:40.667
Mr. proprietor.
Ah! My fake mustache fell.

00:04:40.667 --> 00:04:43.634
I mean, my real mustache.

00:04:43.634 --> 00:04:45.367
[ Normal voice ] Also, how do
you get minions that loyal.

00:04:45.367 --> 00:04:47.300
They committed crimes
for this dude.

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:49.400
The closest thing
I have to a minion is Wally,

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:52.367
and I'm pretty sure
he thinks I'm his minion.

00:04:52.367 --> 00:04:54.067
-You're doing great, kid.

00:04:54.067 --> 00:04:55.901
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.501 --> 00:05:01.701
-Also, it really helps
that Cohen has more credibility

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:03.300
than most of Trump's
usual goons.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:04.834
Like, if Rudy Giuliani
or Mike Lindell

00:05:04.834 --> 00:05:06.334
or Sidney Powell
testify against Trump,

00:05:06.334 --> 00:05:07.801
it probably wouldn't even
hurt him that much,

00:05:07.801 --> 00:05:10.834
because a jury would think
even Trump couldn't have thought

00:05:10.834 --> 00:05:13.334
these lunatics knew anything
about voting machine technology.

00:05:13.334 --> 00:05:14.567
Michael Cohen.

00:05:14.567 --> 00:05:16.734
Michael Cohen
looks exactly like a dude

00:05:16.734 --> 00:05:19.234
you would hire
for help cooking the books.

00:05:19.234 --> 00:05:20.567
If he had a billboard,
it would say...

00:05:22.834 --> 00:05:24.067
[ Laughter ]

00:05:24.067 --> 00:05:25.701
And then there
was the breaking news

00:05:25.701 --> 00:05:27.667
about Trump's former Chief
of Staff, Mark Meadows.

00:05:27.667 --> 00:05:29.501
Meadows was there in
the White House

00:05:29.501 --> 00:05:30.834
with Trump on January 6th,

00:05:30.834 --> 00:05:33.167
and has reportedly
testified multiple times

00:05:33.167 --> 00:05:35.267
in the investigation
of the coup attempt

00:05:35.267 --> 00:05:37.100
by special counsel
Jack Smith.

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:39.767
-Meadows is seen
as a critical witness.

00:05:39.767 --> 00:05:41.467
He was the White House
Chief of Staff,

00:05:41.467 --> 00:05:44.467
and he can offer keen insights
into Trump's actions

00:05:44.467 --> 00:05:46.868
and state of mind
following the election.

00:05:46.868 --> 00:05:50.267
Now, he also allegedly
told investigators

00:05:50.267 --> 00:05:52.968
that he has never seen
any evidence of fraud

00:05:52.968 --> 00:05:56.434
that would keep now President
Joe Biden from the White House,

00:05:56.434 --> 00:05:57.667
and that he agrees

00:05:57.667 --> 00:06:00.801
this was the most secure
election in US history.

00:06:00.801 --> 00:06:03.334
-Meadows also told
federal investigators

00:06:03.334 --> 00:06:06.100
Trump was being,
"dishonest" with the public

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:08.133
when he first claims
to have won the election.

00:06:08.133 --> 00:06:11.367
Hours after polls
closed on November 3, 2020,

00:06:11.367 --> 00:06:15.267
before the final results were
in, "Obviously, we didn't win."

00:06:15.267 --> 00:06:16.501
A source quoted Meadows

00:06:16.501 --> 00:06:19.300
as telling Jack Smith's team
in hindsight.

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:20.801
-You don't get to admit
that you didn't win

00:06:20.801 --> 00:06:22.200
now and three years later,

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:23.868
when you and most of your
cronies are facing jail time.

00:06:23.868 --> 00:06:25.100
Where were you
on election night,

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:26.934
when Trump was scheming
with a whiskey-soaked

00:06:26.934 --> 00:06:29.133
Rudy Giuliani to go out
and claim victory

00:06:29.133 --> 00:06:30.200
before all the votes were in?

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:31.934
Or how Sidney Powell was holding

00:06:31.934 --> 00:06:33.667
her bat [bleep] crazy press
conference,

00:06:33.667 --> 00:06:34.868
wearing the pelt of a leopard

00:06:34.868 --> 00:06:37.367
she claimed had rigged
the election,

00:06:37.367 --> 00:06:39.734
along with China
and the ghost of Hugo Chavez.

00:06:39.734 --> 00:06:41.000
[ As Sidney Powell ]
I personally killed

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.767
this leopard myself
when I found him

00:06:42.767 --> 00:06:45.734
trying to vote
for Joe Biden in Pennsylvania.

00:06:45.734 --> 00:06:47.601
Sorry, leopard,
but you're not 18,

00:06:47.601 --> 00:06:51.601
and now you're never
going to be.

00:06:51.601 --> 00:06:52.734
[ Normal voice ]
I hope the special counsel

00:06:52.734 --> 00:06:54.067
got a lot more information
from Meadows,

00:06:54.067 --> 00:06:56.467
because Meadows
definitely knows a lot more.

00:06:56.467 --> 00:06:57.534
For example,
you might remember

00:06:57.534 --> 00:06:59.801
that Meadows' aide
Cassidy Hutchinson

00:06:59.801 --> 00:07:01.968
testified before
the January 6th Committee.

00:07:01.968 --> 00:07:04.534
Hutchinson revealed
that as the mob

00:07:04.534 --> 00:07:06.033
was rampaging
through the Capitol,

00:07:06.033 --> 00:07:07.501
chanting hang Mike Pence,

00:07:07.501 --> 00:07:11.734
Meadows confirmed that Trump
agreed with the mob.

00:07:11.734 --> 00:07:13.267
-We have some remarkable
new accounts

00:07:13.267 --> 00:07:16.968
of just how explicitly
Donald Trump encouraged violence

00:07:16.968 --> 00:07:19.300
on that day
and in its wake.

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:21.467
One of those accounts
comes from a new book

00:07:21.467 --> 00:07:23.634
written by the former aide
to Trump Chief of Staff

00:07:23.634 --> 00:07:25.634
Mark Meadows,
that's Cassidy Hutchinson.

00:07:25.634 --> 00:07:28.601
In this excerpt highlighted
by my colleague Rachel Maddow

00:07:28.601 --> 00:07:31.467
ahead of her interview with
Cassie Hutchinson last night,

00:07:31.467 --> 00:07:33.534
Hutchinson describes a scene

00:07:33.534 --> 00:07:36.200
from the afternoon
of January 6th,

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:38.367
after news has broken
that the rioters

00:07:38.367 --> 00:07:39.534
have breached the Capitol.

00:08:00.534 --> 00:08:02.100
-I can't wait to hear
Trump's excuse

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:04.868
for yelling the word
"hang" as the mob

00:08:04.868 --> 00:08:06.801
was on TV
ransacking the Capitol,

00:08:06.801 --> 00:08:08.968
literally chanting
they wanted to hang Mike Pence.

00:08:08.968 --> 00:08:10.567
[ As Donald Trump ] I wasn't
saying hang Mike Pence,

00:08:10.567 --> 00:08:12.801
I was saying
"Hangin' with Mr. Cooper,"

00:08:12.801 --> 00:08:14.167
My favorite...

00:08:14.167 --> 00:08:17.133
My favorite '90s TV.
Where are my '90s kids at?

00:08:17.133 --> 00:08:19.868
We all -- We all love
Mr. Cooper, don't we folks?

00:08:19.868 --> 00:08:24.334
That was part of the TGIF block
on ABC.

00:08:24.334 --> 00:08:25.567
T-GIF, as I called it,

00:08:25.567 --> 00:08:27.901
along with "Boy Meets World"
and "Full House."

00:08:27.901 --> 00:08:31.367
You know,
I once met Dave Coulier once.

00:08:31.367 --> 00:08:33.234
He came up to me,
big guy, funny guy,

00:08:33.234 --> 00:08:36.667
tears pouring down his face

00:08:36.667 --> 00:08:38.667
and onto his tacky
brightly colored shirt.

00:08:38.667 --> 00:08:41.234
And he said to me, he said,
"Sir, those radical,

00:08:41.234 --> 00:08:44.767
those radical woke Democrats
need to cut it out."

00:08:44.767 --> 00:08:47.200
[ Laughter ]

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:48.467
They do.

00:08:48.467 --> 00:08:51.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:51.033 --> 00:08:53.100
He was very --
He was very unkind to Alanis.

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:56.868
You need to know that about him?
You oughta know.

00:08:56.868 --> 00:08:58.868
[ Laughter ]

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:01.501
[ Normal voice ]
But at the very least,

00:09:01.501 --> 00:09:02.834
we have the president's
chief of staff

00:09:02.834 --> 00:09:05.033
now reportedly confirming
that he knew the entire time

00:09:05.033 --> 00:09:06.667
the election fraud stuff
was all [bleep].

00:09:06.667 --> 00:09:08.334
And, yet, the election
deniers nonetheless

00:09:08.334 --> 00:09:10.200
remain the core
of the current Republican Party.

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:11.601
That's who controls the party,

00:09:11.601 --> 00:09:14.467
as evidenced by their selection
today of a new speaker,

00:09:14.467 --> 00:09:16.634
a far-right conservative
who almost no one

00:09:16.634 --> 00:09:18.334
has heard of named Mike Johnson.

00:09:18.334 --> 00:09:19.434
I think they're hoping to bore

00:09:19.434 --> 00:09:21.234
everyone into forgetting
how extreme he is.

00:09:21.234 --> 00:09:22.701
Mike Johnson is the fake name

00:09:22.701 --> 00:09:24.868
they give you
when you call tech support.

00:09:24.868 --> 00:09:27.400
So it sounds like you're talking
to someone in Kansas

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:30.501
when you're definitely talking
to someone in Albania.

00:09:30.501 --> 00:09:31.968
[ Albanian accent ]
Yes, I am Mike Johnson.

00:09:31.968 --> 00:09:35.067
Did you try unplug
and plug in again?

00:09:35.067 --> 00:09:36.267
[ Normal voice ]
Even his fellow Republicans

00:09:36.267 --> 00:09:37.367
didn't know much about him.

00:09:37.367 --> 00:09:39.033
Senator Susan Collins,
and this is true,

00:09:39.033 --> 00:09:40.634
said she'd have to look him up.

00:09:40.634 --> 00:09:42.067
A reporter from CNN wrote
today...

00:09:49.267 --> 00:09:50.567
[ Laughter ]

00:09:50.567 --> 00:09:52.200
Well, when you Google him,
you're going to need

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:55.734
to put in more information
than just the name Mike Johnson.

00:09:55.734 --> 00:09:57.634
Mike Johnson
is such a common name.

00:09:57.634 --> 00:10:00.801
Most of us went to school
with one.

00:10:00.801 --> 00:10:02.267
My Mike Johnson
played baseball.

00:10:02.267 --> 00:10:04.100
This Mike Johnson played
a key role

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:06.300
in the effort to overturn
the 2020 election results

00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:07.501
and was, according to
The New York Times...

00:10:10.167 --> 00:10:11.334
...on January 6th.

00:10:11.334 --> 00:10:13.133
But Republicans desperately

00:10:13.133 --> 00:10:15.300
do not want to talk
about that,

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:17.400
as evidenced by this
press conference last night

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:20.167
where a reporter tried
to ask Mike Fake Name

00:10:20.167 --> 00:10:22.467
about his effort
to overturn the election,

00:10:22.467 --> 00:10:24.400
and the group
of Republicans assembled

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:26.234
literally booed the reporter.

00:10:31.667 --> 00:10:34.667
-[ Booing ]

00:10:35.868 --> 00:10:36.901
-Next question.

00:10:36.901 --> 00:10:38.300
-Oh, grow up!

00:10:38.300 --> 00:10:39.334
[ Laughter ]

00:10:39.334 --> 00:10:40.968
You're booing
like a bunch of kids

00:10:40.968 --> 00:10:42.767
at a production
of "PAW Patrol" on ice

00:10:42.767 --> 00:10:45.133
when Mayor Humdinger comes out.

00:10:45.133 --> 00:10:47.000
[ As Mayor Humdinger ]
Oh, wait until I get my hands

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:48.467
on those pesky pups.

00:10:48.467 --> 00:10:50.567
[ Imitates children booing ]

00:10:50.567 --> 00:10:53.100
[ Laughter ]

00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:56.200
[ Normal voice ] Went and saw
"PAW Patrol" two this weekend.

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:57.234
Woof!

00:10:57.234 --> 00:10:59.234
[ Laughter ]

00:11:01.767 --> 00:11:04.868
In retrospect, I should have --
I should have taken my kids.

00:11:04.868 --> 00:11:06.901
[ Laughter ]

00:11:06.901 --> 00:11:08.234
[ Applause ]

00:11:08.234 --> 00:11:09.901
They wanted to see
"Killers of the Flower Moon."

00:11:09.901 --> 00:11:11.334
[ Laughter ]

00:11:11.334 --> 00:11:12.367
and I'm like,
"That's too long.

00:11:12.367 --> 00:11:13.434
I'm going to go see
'PAW Patrol.'"

00:11:13.434 --> 00:11:15.467
But then that backfires

00:11:15.467 --> 00:11:16.567
because this is, like,
90 minutes.

00:11:16.567 --> 00:11:18.501
I got to sit in
the [bleep] lobby.

00:11:18.501 --> 00:11:19.834
[ Laughter ]

00:11:22.901 --> 00:11:24.734
I mean, can you imagine
having the gall

00:11:24.734 --> 00:11:26.701
to boo someone for asking
a simple question

00:11:26.701 --> 00:11:28.734
after you paralyze
the government for three weeks

00:11:28.734 --> 00:11:31.000
of spectacle
and humiliating incompetence,

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:32.367
where you screamed
and yelled at each other

00:11:32.367 --> 00:11:34.100
like a bunch of street pigeons

00:11:34.100 --> 00:11:35.400
fighting over a French fry.

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:36.567
You booed the reporter.

00:11:36.567 --> 00:11:38.033
That's like going
to a football stadium

00:11:38.033 --> 00:11:40.601
and getting booed
by the Giants.

00:11:40.601 --> 00:11:41.701
[ Laughter ]

00:11:41.701 --> 00:11:43.968
Do I boo you when you vape

00:11:43.968 --> 00:11:46.901
and get too handsy
at "Beetlejuice" the musical?

00:11:46.901 --> 00:11:49.834
No, I get an usher
like an adult.

00:11:49.834 --> 00:11:51.067
[ Laughter ]

00:11:51.067 --> 00:11:54.167
Also, can we zoom in
on this kindly older woman

00:11:54.167 --> 00:11:57.167
up front to hear
what she had to say?

00:11:57.167 --> 00:11:59.000
-Shut up!

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:01.133
Shut up.

00:12:01.133 --> 00:12:03.200
That's North Carolina
Congress monster

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:05.300
and election denier,
Virginia Fox.

00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:07.734
And maybe steer clear of
her house on Halloween, kids,

00:12:07.734 --> 00:12:10.067
because I'm pretty sure
it's going to be raisins.

00:12:10.067 --> 00:12:11.501
[ Laughter ]

00:12:11.501 --> 00:12:13.100
And yet, even after
they spent three weeks

00:12:13.100 --> 00:12:14.868
humiliating themselves
and breaking the government,

00:12:14.868 --> 00:12:17.033
Republicans actually celebrated
when they finally managed

00:12:17.033 --> 00:12:19.701
to do the single basic
aspect of their jobs,

00:12:19.701 --> 00:12:22.000
like they had just landed
a rover on Mars.

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:23.901
Maybe instead
of patting themselves

00:12:23.901 --> 00:12:25.667
on the backs
and yelling at reporters,

00:12:25.667 --> 00:12:28.167
you guys should at least
have the decency to...

00:12:28.167 --> 00:12:29.634
-Shut up.

00:12:29.634 --> 00:12:30.868
[ Laughter ]

00:12:30.868 --> 00:12:32.534
-This has been A Closer Look.

00:12:32.534 --> 00:12:35.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

